{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And he spoke to the congregation, saying.</b> The meaning of <b>saying</b> is that he should say to them that thus was said to him from the mouth of the Holy One, blessed be He, to say to them:" "<b>Turn aside, please, from the tents of these wicked men.</b> Moses, peace be upon him, employed wisdom to bring them merit through the pleasantness of his words, by the means that they would appraise them at the value of wicked men — and this is his saying <b>these wicked men</b>: meaning, that they should be in their eyes at the value of wicked men and turn away from them, for they would believe in their destruction and fear lest evil cleave to them; and as reward for this HaShem would grant them favor. And although HaShem was already appeased to say to them ״Go up,״ nevertheless the righteous desire to justify the people of their generation, that they may eat of the fruit of their way."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:24.953366628Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}